Package: devjam-system-config-rtirq
Version: 1.0-1
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: rtirq
Breaks: devjam-science-experiment-mode-rtirq (<< 1.47-1~)
Replaces: devjam-science-experiment-mode-rtirq (<< 1.47-1~)
Maintainer: Bob Rosbag <debian@bobrosbag.nl>
Description: Real-time IRQ priorities (rtirq) for deterministic timing
 rtirq configuration for computers with deterministic timing for
 EEG, button boxes and audio-visual stimuli: audio, USB, parallel port
 and Intel GPU interrupts get real-time priorities. /etc/rtirq.conf of
 the rtirq package is diverted and replaced by this configuration.
 rtirq needs threaded IRQs (a PREEMPT_RT kernel or the kernel parameter
 threadirqs). verify-rtirq shows the priorities rtirq set and
 check-rt-processes lists all real-time threads.
 .
 Works on its own, without experiment mode. devjam-science-experiment-mode
 can limit rtirq to experiment mode (switch-rtirq).
